(Objective: Apply last-in-first-out and first-in-first-out rules to a short sequence) Tj T*
(of stored items.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(MOCK ORIGINAL LESSON. A stack removes the most recently added item first: last in,) Tj T*
(first out \(LIFO\). A queue removes the earliest waiting item first: first in, first) Tj T*
(out \(FIFO\). The same stored items can therefore leave in different orders.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(WORKED EXAMPLE) Tj T*
(Add A, then B, then C. In a stack, the next removal returns C because it was added) Tj T*
(last. In a queue, the next removal returns A because it has waited longest. Both) Tj T*
(structures then contain two items; their removal rule, rather than their item count,) Tj T*
(distinguishes them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHECK AND CORRECTION) Tj T*
(An undo history should return the most recent action first. Which structure matches) Tj T*
(that rule?) Tj T*
(A stack returns the latest stored action first. This is a rule-selection example,) Tj T*
(not a full undo implementation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Keep order and count separate. Enqueue adds one item at the back; dequeue removes) Tj T*
(one item from the front. After four additions and two valid removals from a) Tj T*
(previously empty queue, two items remain. A removal from an empty structure is) Tj T*
(outside this example and must be handled explicitly in real software.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(INDEPENDENT APPLICATION) Tj T*
(An empty queue receives four items, then performs two valid removals. How many items) Tj T*
(remain?) Tj T*
(Four additions produce four items. Two removals leave 4 - 2 = 2 items.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(GLOSSARY) Tj T*
(Stack: A structure whose next removal returns the most recently added remaining) Tj T*
(item.) Tj T*
(Queue: A structure whose next removal returns the earliest added remaining item.) Tj T*
(FIFO: First in, first out: the earliest waiting item leaves first.) Tj T*
(LIFO: Last in, first out: the most recently added item leaves first.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Choose the structure from the required removal rule, then trace its operations.) Tj T*
(Stack means latest first; queue means earliest first. State empty-structure behavior) Tj T*
(separately rather than guessing.) Tj T*
